  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Find the $x$-intercepts and $y$-intercepts of the graphs of each of the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p32-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=x^3-x^2-2x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x$-intercepts: $-1,0,2$. $y$-intercept: $0$.",
          "worked": "For the $x$-intercepts, set $y=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^3-x^2-2x&=0\\\\x(x^2-x-2)&=0\\\\x(x-2)(x+1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x=-1,0,2$.\nFor the $y$-intercept, set $x=0$: $y=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=x^3-2x^2-5x+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x$-intercepts: $-2,1,3$. $y$-intercept: $6$.",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-2x^2-5x+6$.\n$$P(1)=1-2-5+6=0.$$\nHence $x-1$ is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(x^2-x-6)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(x-3)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$\nSetting $y=0$ gives $x=-2,1,3$.\nSetting $x=0$ gives $y=6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 59
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q13-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=x^3+2x^2-x-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x$-intercepts: $-2,-1,1$. $y$-intercept: $-2$.",
          "worked": "Factorise by grouping:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=x^2(x+2)-(x+2)\\\\y&=(x+2)(x^2-1)\\\\y&=(x+2)(x-1)(x+1).\\end{align*}$$\nSetting $y=0$ gives $x=-2,-1,1$.\nSetting $x=0$ gives $y=-2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q13-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=3x^3-4x^2-13x-6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x$-intercepts: $-1,-\\frac23,3$. $y$-intercept: $-6$.",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=3x^3-4x^2-13x-6$.\n$$P(-1)=-3-4+13-6=0.$$\nHence $x+1$ is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(3x^2-7x-6)\\\\P(x)&=(x+1)(3x^2-9x+2x-6)\\\\P(x)&=(x+1)(x-3)(3x+2).\\end{align*}$$\nSetting $y=0$ gives $x=-1,-\\frac23,3$.\nSetting $x=0$ gives $y=-6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q13-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$y=5x^3+12x^2-36x-16$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x$-intercepts: $-4,-\\frac25,2$. $y$-intercept: $-16$.",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=5x^3+12x^2-36x-16$.\n$$P(2)=40+48-72-16=0.$$\nHence $x-2$ is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-2)(5x^2+22x+8)\\\\P(x)&=(x-2)(5x^2+20x+2x+8)\\\\P(x)&=(x-2)(x+4)(5x+2).\\end{align*}$$\nSetting $y=0$ gives $x=-4,-\\frac25,2$.\nSetting $x=0$ gives $y=-16$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q13-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$y=6x^3-5x^2-2x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x$-intercepts: $-\\frac12,\\frac13,1$. $y$-intercept: $1$.",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=6x^3-5x^2-2x+1$.\n$$P(1)=6-5-2+1=0.$$\nHence $x-1$ is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(6x^2+x-1)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(6x^2+3x-2x-1)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(2x+1)(3x-1).\\end{align*}$$\nSetting $y=0$ gives $x=-\\frac12,\\frac13,1$.\nSetting $x=0$ gives $y=1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      }
    ]
  },
